    {
      "id": "twilite-product-hero",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "✨ Promise",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 680,
        "y": -80
      },
      "width": 620,
      "height": 250,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#111827",
        "color": "#f8fafc",
        "borderColor": "#5b8cff",
        "borderWidth": 2,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 24
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# ✨ Build Knowledge As A Living Graph\n\nTwilite turns graphs into durable web artifacts that humans and AI can both navigate, edit, and grow together.\n\nNot a canvas snapshot. Not a disposable chat. A structured system that stays alive as the work gets deeper.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "layout",
          "updatedAt": 1778698422220,
          "reason": "auto-layout"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "twilite-product-difference",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "🧭 Why Twilite Exists",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 1340,
        "y": -80
      },
      "width": 540,
      "height": 250,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#1f2937",
        "color": "#f8fafc",
        "borderColor": "#fb923c",
        "borderWidth": 2,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 24
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "## 🧭 Why Twilite Exists\n\nMost tools split thinking across chats, docs, tabs, whiteboards, and disconnected notes.\n\nTwilite keeps the structure itself in view.\n\nThe graph becomes the thing with value: addressable, inspectable, editable, and durable on the web.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1778699868381,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "twilite-product-how",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "⚙️ How It Works",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 680,
        "y": 240
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 240,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#0f172a",
        "color": "#e2e8f0",
        "borderColor": "#64748b",
        "borderWidth": 2,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 22
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "## ⚙️ How It Works\n\n1. Author or evolve a graph.\n2. Give it a durable address.\n3. Let humans and AI work against the same structure over time.\n\nThat lets a graph move from thought, to collaboration, to publishing, to execution without changing mediums.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "layout",
          "updatedAt": 1778698422220,
          "reason": "auto-layout"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "twilite-product-proof",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "🧪 Proof",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 1240,
        "y": 240
      },
      "width": 620,
      "height": 250,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
